[style name="Interaction_Style"]
join Thorinn (normal) leftmost
if {Hugo.Followed_to_rockfall} == false:
	Thorinn: This must be Hugo's inn.
	Narrator: *knock knock*
	join Hugo rightmost
	[signal arg="show_hugo"]
	Hugo: [i]Look who we have here[/i], seems like you've found your way.
join Hugo rightmost
Hugo: Come on in, I'll get you your room ready.
leave --All--
[signal arg="start_night"]
[wait time="2.0"]
Narrator: *Thorinn spends the night at the inn*
[signal arg="change_to_day_light"]
[signal arg="end-night"]
[wait time="2.0"]
join Thorinn leftmost
join Hugo rightmost
Hugo: Morning, traveler! How was your sleep?
Thorinn: It was good. The bed was a welcome change after spending days in the woods.
Hugo: Glad to hear. What brings you to Rockfall?
Thorinn: Mhhh...
Thorinn: I’m a [i]doctor[/i]. I thought a remote village like this might benefit from my skills. Medical knowledge can be hard to come by in places like this.
Hugo: Hmm... What a [i]coincidence[/i]. Ian, our pharmacist, has fallen ill. Perhaps you could visit him. See if there’s anything you can do to help?
Thorinn: I’d be happy to help. Where can I find him?
Hugo: The pharmacy is the building [b]across[/b] the river. You will recognise it by the sign by the door. The door’s always open.
Hugo: Tell Ian I sent you, he’ll trust you more that way.
Thorinn (surprised): Why [i]wouldn’t[/i] he trust me?
Hugo: This town doesn’t welcome strangers easily. You’ll see soon enough.
[signal arg="Start_Find_Ian"]
